{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.4742884258130768, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. There is no file or network access and no hard-coded answers. Test labels are never used: only Xtr and y go into fitting, and Xte is used only for predict.", "No bug that would make the result meaningless. All randomness comes from the seed argument (seed + 1000*k). The Ridge part does not depend on the seed, so it is computed once and reused in each of the 3 blends, which is correct. Averaging the rank-normalised blends keeps the output at one number per test molecule.", "Recomputed z: (0.4745 - 0.4743) / (0.0070 * sqrt(2)) = 0.0002 / 0.0099 \u2248 0.020, which matches the harness. The gain is about 0.03 noise sd, so it is not detectable.", "This is a non-veto concern. The change roughly triples the cost of fitting the tree models (9 fits per fold instead of 3), which brings the job closer to the 10-minute limit. It also adds code for no measurable gain. Under the 'simpler is better' rule, the provisional reject is appropriate."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Average three seed-derived passes (seed, seed+1000, seed+2000) of the RF, LightGBM and CatBoost blend, with the deterministic Ridge member fitted once, and return the mean of the three rank-normalized blends.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "willow", "idea_id": "b031", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.47448267673864636, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.47448267673864636, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B2_clear_SS_2_s0-candidate-15_1795072218462", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00289064, "cost_usd_plan": 0.00289064, "latency_s": 15.081554664997384, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 7484, "tokens_out": 3314}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0291798, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0291798, "latency_s": 8.83370716200443, "requ